libemf2svg: https://github.com/kakwa/libemf2svg
Revision: 658a718de180666d342a78fd4046ec1f41e65e17 (1.8.1)
License: GPL-2.0; see LICENSE. libuemf and fmem retain their own license notices.

This subset contains the static converter, its libuemf implementation, and fmem
for Windows. Unix platforms use native open_memstream. PNG, FreeType, Fontconfig and iconv use existing dependencies.
The converter does not use libxml2. CLI, argp, vcpkg, demos and build tools are omitted.
EMF+ sources remain because the converter references their record handlers.

KiCad supplies a target-scoped CMake build and disables DLL exports for static use.

Local conversion patches accept a caller-owned Fontconfig configuration, map
LOGFONT weights correctly, and retain Calibri's blank glyph when fonts substitute.
Text output preserves character advances, vertical advances, and baseline rotation.
Malformed text spans and unmapped glyphs fail conversion; glyph lookup and record
headers are checked before reading. Reverse maps use bounded font glyph counts.
The bundled libuemf record validator runs before record analysis and conversion.
Local fixes check text offsets before dereferencing and retain wide count arithmetic.
The upstream validator does not inspect payloads of record types marked unimplemented.

Windows memory streams reject path/access errors instead of retrying forever.

Bitmap validation checks full padded rows, declared metadata spans, and extended-header palettes. RLE
bitmaps are rejected so callers can retain their WMF fallback.
